content:
Help me define bounded contexts. Below I will provide domain information. 

#### Data:
These are the extracted objects and the subdomain grouping:
```json
{
  "domain objects": [
    {
      "name": "Seller",
      "description": "Person offering an item for auction."
    },
    {
      "name": "Listing",
      "description": "Public posting that offers an item for auction.",
      "attributes": [
        "Item"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Item",
      "description": "Object being auctioned.",
      "attributes": [
        "Item Description"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Item Description",
      "description": "Details that describe the item."
    },
    {
      "name": "Bidder",
      "description": "Person placing bids on auctioned items."
    },
    {
      "name": "Bid",
      "description": "Offer from a bidder to purchase the item."
    },
    {
      "name": "Auction Manager",
      "description": "Person overseeing auction setup and bidding."
    },
    {
      "name": "Auction",
      "description": "Process in which bidders compete for the item.",
      "attributes": [
        "Item",
        "Scheduled Time",
        "Winner"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Scheduled Time",
      "description": "Planned start time of the auction."
    },
    {
      "name": "Winner",
      "description": "Bidder who wins the auction."
    },
    {
      "name": "Shipping Officer",
      "description": "Person coordinating delivery to the winner."
    },
    {
      "name": "Delivery",
      "description": "Transfer of the sold item to the winning bidder.",
      "attributes": [
        "Item",
        "Winner"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```
```json
{
  "subdomains": {
    "Auctioning": {
      "objects": [
        "Bidder",
        "Auction Manger",
        "Bid",
        "Auction",
        "Item",
        "Scheduled Time",
        "Winner"
      ]
    },
    "Item Listing": {
      "objects": [
        "Seller",
        "Listing",
        "Item",
        "Item Description"
      ]
    },
    "Item Delivery": {
      "objects": [
        "Shipping Officer",
        "Delivery",
        "Item",
        "Winner"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

#### Task:
- Assign the subdomains to bounded contexts. 
- Name the subdomain the bounded context might be derived from, it might also be multiple.
- In case an object appears in multiple bounded contexts, suggest a name change.
- Also suggest a name change if the meaning of the object is too similar to an object from another bounded context
- Return the bounded contexts in json format. Here is an example for structuring the data:
```json
{
  "bounded contexts": {
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": []
    },
    "...": {
      "derived from": "...",
      "objects": [
        "...",
        "...",
        "..."
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "... -> ..."
      ]
    }
  }
}
```

Here are the bounded contexts: 
```json
{
  "bounded contexts": {
    "Auctioning": {
      "derived from": "Auctioning Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Bidder",
        "Auction Manager",
        "Bid",
        "Auction",
        "Auction Item",
        "Scheduled Time",
        "Winner"
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "Item -> Auction Item"
      ]
    },
    "Item Listing": {
      "derived from": "Item Listing Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Seller",
        "Listing",
        "Item",
        "Item Description"
      ],
      "name changes": []
    },
    "Item Delivery": {
      "derived from": "Item Delivery Subdomain",
      "objects": [
        "Shipping Officer",
        "Delivery",
        "Shipped Item",
        "Recipient"
      ],
      "name changes": [
        "Item -> Shipped Item",
        "Winner -> Recipient"
      ]
    }
  }
}
```
